nce.", "wall_independence_note": "No behavioural DV is measured (no approach rate, latency, or choice). The 514-family / EXP-0098 substrate ceiling therefore cannot be re-derived by this design; its DVs read the substrate's own node store and prioritisation function.", "known_substrate_defect_note": "FIXED before this run -- recorded so the defect's history is legible, NOT as a live finding. ree_core/agent.py::_do_replay used to build a 4-element drive_state against a VALENCE_DIM=6 field (widened by MECH-307, 2026-05-11), so the agent-level valence-weighted replay entry point raised RuntimeError with no try/except; the defect was found by this experiment's own Step 2.5a substrate probe on 2026-08-03. As of ree-v3 32edd553 (2026-08-04) _do_replay builds the vector BY INDEX at VALENCE_DIM with the MECH-307 split-surprise slots (4,5) deliberately zero-weighted in both flag states, and ResidueField.get_valence_priority zero-pads-and-records a legacy narrow vector instead of raising. Pinned by tests/contracts/test_do_replay_drive_state_width.py. do_replay_drive_state_width_probe now MEASURES the live path per seed (spying on the hippocampal replay entry points and on get_valence_priority) rather than restating the old construction, so it stands as a regression witness: because the pad means a re-narrowing would no longer raise, pad_count_delta is the only thing that would notice. SD-014's own claim (the node vector and priority(node)=dot(V,d)) is exercised here with a correctly sized vector either way.", "custom_information": {"probe_2026_08_03": "Step 2.5a probe confirmed all four SD-014 channels populate (WANTING 21 / LIKING 18 / HARM_DISC 24 / SURPRISE 26 nodes over 12 episodes at num_resources=5) and that surprise_write_count=616, lifting the EVB-0245 blocked_substrate blocks (1) and (2).", "gov_reuse_1_check": "Decisive readout = C1/C2/C3 valence-discrimination stats (mean pairwise Kendall tau, |Spearman(w,l)|, top-K Jaccard) under a STRONGER-THAN-DEFAULT incentive-sensitization gain (rate 0.10 / max 8.0 / coupling 2.5). This is a NEW manipulation: no recorded run carries these gain values. The nearest predecessors 887 (default write-path, no sensitization) and 887a (default gain 0.05/4.0/1.0) both recorded the readout but at DIFFERENT operating points, so their numbers answer a different question and cannot be reused. The stronger-gain readout is neither recorded nor derivable post-hoc (the gain changes the WANTING write at accumulation time, not a reprocessing of stored valence). Not recoverable -> run."}, "non_degenerate": true, "degeneracy_reason": "", "degenerate_metrics": {}, "recording_schema": "rec/v1", "substrate_hash": "9ee0197be74bd0392cf8d953992184722d877b3881b70ab6007a0fe3fe6d78d5", "substrate_commit": {"commit": "b08cc1575ea3f28ecd51f937984733c3878c4aad", "dirty": false, "branch": "main"}, "substrate_stable_across_run": true, "substrate_identity": {"source": "manifest_write_disk_read", "resolved_at_utc": "2026-08-08T09:51:01Z", "commit_source": "manifest_write_disk_read", "commit_resolved_at_utc": "2026-08-08T09:51:01Z", "stamped_at_utc": "2026-08-08T09:51:01Z", "lag_seconds": 0, "stability_snapshots": 1, "drifted_since_resolved": false}, "z_goal_stream": {"ticks_total": 11883, "ticks_active": 0, "writer_calls": 11883, "active_frac": 0.0, "writer_defect": false, "n_agents": 3, "goal_state_present": true}, "machine": "ree-worker-1", "machine_class": "linux-x86_64-py3.10-torch2.12.0+cpu", "elapsed_seconds": 1501.36573978886, "config": {"tau_max": 0.85, "rho_max": 0.9, "jaccard_max": 0.8, "top_k": 5, "channel_nodes_floor": 8, "node_floor": 8, "comparable_pairs_floor": 10, "tau_control_ceil": 0.5, "control_nodes": 16, "rollout_episodes": 40, "steps_per_episode": 120, "seeds": [42, 137, 2026], "env": {"size": 10, "num_hazards": 3, "num_resources": 6, "hazard_harm": 0.5, "resource_benefit": 0.3, "use_proxy_fields": true}, "alpha_world": 0.9, "tonic_5ht_enabled": true, "valence_harm_enabled": true, "valence_liking_enabl